"c": "In this unit, you have been introduced to the basic logical structures that characterize structured programming. A very major objective of structured programming as you have learnt in this unit is to increase program clarity by reducing complexity. This is the fundamental principle behind the use of modular approach and top-down technique in structured programming. The three basic control structure, c: patterns employed in structured programming are Sequence, Selection and Iterative structures. The illustrative flowcharts for these patterns were presented in this unit.",
