"s": "Merge sort adopts the strategy of divide-and- conquer. It requires dividing the array into two halves and sorting them recursively, then merging the two smaller sorted arrays into a single one. Merge sort algorithm is divided into two- the merge sort( for splitting and sorting halves ) and the merger( for merging two halves together). 6.0TUTOR -MARKED ASSIGNMENT 1. Apply merge sort to sort the list E, X, A, M, P. L. E in alphabetical order.\n2. How stable is the divide-and-conquer algorithm? 237 PROGRAMMING AND ALGORITHMS",
